law.text:
		The Secretaries of Health and Human Resources and Education shall work together in:

Promoting interagency consensus and facilitating complementary agency positions on issues relating to early intervention services;


Examining and evaluating the effectiveness of state agency programs, services, and plans for early intervention services and identifying duplications, inefficiencies, and unmet needs;


Analyzing state agency budget requests and any other budget items affecting early intervention services;


Proposing ways of realigning funding to promote interagency initiatives and programs for early intervention services;


Formulating recommendations on planning, priorities, and expenditures for early intervention services and communicating the recommendations to the Governor and state agency heads;


Formulating joint policy positions and statements on legislative issues regarding early intervention services and communicating those positions and statements to the General Assembly; and


Resolving interagency disputes and assigning financial responsibility in accordance with Part C of the Individuals with Disabilities Education Act (20 U.S.C. § 1431 et seq.).
